From df66b3d522a0bb2080235fd88c648b9168513b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:52:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: show one address pill while the bar morphs into the tab
 sheet

The address pill on screen is the compositor toolbar texture, so hiding
the location bar view did not remove it, and the glass sheet window was
placed one layout late. While the bottom-bar sheet opened, the real pill
and the travelling morph pill were both visible.

The morph now waits until the glass window covers the bar, starts at
the measured bar rect, hides the address views (INVISIBLE, not GONE) and
suppresses the toolbar scene layer in the same step through a new
ToolbarManager hook, which also drops the cached toolbar bitmap. A
toolbar-coloured cover hides the last texture frame for a few frames.

The glass window attributes are posted when they change during layout,
which fixes an input-dispatch ANR. Top-bar sheet and side drawer are
unchanged.
